      "kind": "rationale",
      "line": 393,
      "obj_id": "docs/wayland/WLD-02-INPUT-CONFORMANCE-RELEASE.md#0.1.0-rationale",
      "text": "Wayland input contains capability loss, cancellation, arbitrary touch IDs,\nmodifier state, and axis units that do not map mechanically onto current rlvgl\nevents. A phase-level contract prevents silent lossy behavior while keeping\nthe initial backend small and avoiding concurrent changes to MPY, CPython, or\nLPAR-owned public semantics."
